From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: git: harden the context snapshot and branch lookup

At the first prompt zcode runs git rev-parse, status and log in the
working directory, before any approval. A repository can commit a bare
repository layout (HEAD, objects/, refs/, config) in a subdirectory;
started there, git discovers it and status runs its core.fsmonitor.
Pass -c safe.bareRepository=explicit -c core.fsmonitor=false
-c log.showSignature=false to these calls, to the TUI's branch lookup
and to the git reads of dynamic workflows.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/adapters/src/context/git-snapshot.ts	2026-09-25 15:59:56.761002745 +0200
